# Copy to .env.local for local frontend dev. Every .env* name here is gitignored except this
# template — see the root .gitignore.
# Vite proxies /api/v1 for same-origin cookies — see vite.config.ts. The /uploads entry beside it
# went with the static mount in E3-S1d-3 (#112); documents are served by the API now.
VITE_API_URL=/api/v1

# --- API proxy target (Render / remote NestJS) ---
# Vercel frontend project: set API_PROXY_TARGET in the Vercel dashboard (never commit the URL).
#   Example value: https://your-service.onrender.com
# Local dev (optional): point Vite proxy at Render instead of localhost:3001
# API_PROXY_TARGET=https://your-service.onrender.com
# SBR_API_PROXY_TARGET=https://your-service.onrender.com

# --- Public web surface (E8-S4) ---
# The canonical origin this deployment speaks for. It is what canonical links, Open Graph URLs and
# the sitemap point at, so it has to be the address the public actually visits and not the internal
# one. Leave it unset and the default in src/lib/seo.ts is used. Set it on the production Vercel
# project; leave it off preview deployments, because a preview that claims the production origin is
# asking to be indexed in its place. robots.txt and sitemap.xml are generated per request and read
# the host that asked, so they stay correct on whatever hostname serves them either way.
# VITE_SITE_URL=https://safebuyrealties-app.vercel.app

# --- Feature flags (CH-1) ---
# The browser reads its flags from GET /api/v1/feature-flags, so the way to turn a feature on is
# to set FEATURE_<KEY> on the API, not here. These variables are the state of the page before that
# response arrives and the answer for a key the API did not send. The API wins once it answers.
# Vite inlines them at build time, so changing one means a rebuild, which is exactly why they are
# not the authority.
# VITE_FEATURE_PAYOUTS=off
# VITE_FEATURE_KYC_GATE=off
